window.docContents[190].resolve({"/Distance/#section-the-girth-of-the-hypercube":{"contents":"The hypercube is triangle-free (hypercube_cliqueFree_three), so its girth is at\nleast 4, and for n ≥ 2 it contains a 4-cycle: in Q[2] the Gray-code\nHamiltonian cycle grayCycle 0 of Exercises Walks is one. Each\nlarger cube contains a copy of the previous one, via the embedding\nhypercube.embedFalse, and a graph containing a copy of H has girth at most that\nof H (Mathlib's IsContained.egirth_le).\n\nlemma egirth_hypercube {n : ℕ} : egirth Q[n + 2] = 4 := by\n  refine le_antisymm ?_\n    (four_le_egirth_of_cliqueFree_three (hypercube_cliqueFree_three _))\n  induction n with\n  | zero => exact (grayCycle_isHamiltonianCycle 0).isCycle.egirth_le_length\n  | succ n ih =>\n    exact (IsContained.egirth_le ⟨(hypercube.embedFalse _).toCopy⟩).trans ih\n\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Distance\u0009Girth","header":"11.3.3. The Girth of the Hypercube","id":"/Distance/#section-the-girth-of-the-hypercube"}});